# No decorative box glow (ask when unclear)

**Load** [`.agents/skills/no-box-glow/SKILL.md`](../../.agents/skills/no-box-glow/SKILL.md) when designing glow, bloom, soft light, or decorative shadow.

## Default

**Do not** add decorative `box-shadow`, soft box blurs, or glow for polish (AABB haze looks ugly on rotated marks).

Allowed without asking: design-system elevation, focus rings, borders/radius, and intentional **`ex-glowing-*`** chart recipes (ECharts series light).

## When glow/shadow context is unclear

**Ask the user first** — what shape glows, soft vs sharp, shape-outline vs rectangular chip.

If approved: SVG `feGaussianBlur` / `drop-shadow` on the real geometry; keep glow **outside** `mask` / `overflow: hidden`. Never `box-shadow` on a rotated diamond/chip.
